//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Version 1.12.0 "Puente de Santiago" - May 02, 2026

Recommended Versions:
- Make sure Catch 2 v3 is installed in your system
- Boost version 1.90 or higher is required
- CMake version 3.27 or higher is required
- GCC is recommended to be at least version 13, clang should be at least version 18.
  Earlier versions might work if C++20 is sufficiently supported
- We suggest to use Ubuntu 24.04 LTS or 26.04 LTS as the host platform if you plan
  to use the CUDA example.

********************** INCOMPATIBILITIES / PLEASE NOTE *************************

- Static linking support (BUILDSTATIC / GENEVA_STATIC / GENEVA_STATIC=TRUE) has
  been removed. Geneva now builds exclusively as shared libraries. Any build scripts
  that set BUILDSTATIC="1" or pass -DGENEVA_STATIC=TRUE must be updated to remove
  that setting. The five Geneva shared libraries (gemfony-common, gemfony-hap,
  gemfony-courtier, gemfony-geneva, gemfony-geneva-individuals) are always built
  as SHARED; BUILD_SHARED_LIBS is always ON; GEM_DYNAMIC is always defined.
- gemfony_exception was renamed to geneva_exception (~128 files). Any user code that
  catches or explicitly names this exception type must be updated accordingly.
- The Boost.Test library linkage has been removed from the build-system, instead Geneva now
  uses Catch2 v3 which needs to be present on the system in order to compile the code.
- Windows and macOS support has been removed. Geneva now targets Linux exclusively.
  The G_API_COMMON, G_API_HAP, G_API_COURTIER, G_API_GENEVA, and G_API_INDIVIDUALS
  symbol-visibility macros have been removed from all 2266 call sites and from
  GGlobalDefines.hpp entirely (they were no-ops on Linux without -fvisibility=hidden).
  The GEM_*_EXPORTS preprocessor definitions and the GEM_DYNAMIC definition have been
  removed from the CMake build system. The PLATFORM_NEEDS_LIBRARY_LINKING variable
  always evaluates to FALSE and its conditional TARGET_LINK_LIBRARIES blocks have been
  removed from all five library CMakeLists.txt files. IdentifySystemParameters.cmake
  now supports only GCC >= 13 and Clang >= 18 on Linux.

************************* Noteworthy Changes ***********************************

- Build system stripped to Linux-only: IdentifySystemParameters.cmake, all four
  CommonGenevaBuild.cmake copies, and the five library CMakeLists.txt files have been
  cleaned of Windows (MSVC, Cygwin), macOS (AppleClang, Darwin), Intel compiler, and
  FreeBSD branches. The cmake configure step is now ~150 lines shorter with no dead
  platform-conditional branches.

- GCanvas (the PPM-image canvas used by the Mona-Lisa CUDA example) has been
  moved from the Common library (include/common/GCanvas.hpp, src/common/GCanvas.cpp,
  namespace Gem::Common) into example 15 (examples/geneva/15_GCUDAWorker/GCanvas.hpp
  / GCanvas.cpp, namespace Gem::Geneva). GCanvas is not a general-purpose library
  component; moving it keeps the Common library free of application-specific code.
  The old manual test in tests/common/ManualTests/GCanvasTest/ and the deprecated
  OpenCL sources in examples/geneva/15_GCUDAWorker/Deprecated/ have been removed.
  A new test subdirectory (examples/geneva/15_GCUDAWorker/tests/) holds the
  Catch2 unit tests (GCanvasTests) and a manual smoke-test (GCanvasTest). GCanvas
  unit tests have been removed from GCommonStandardTests.cpp and now live with
  example 15. GCanvas test coverage: coord2D (construction, operator-, dot product);
  GRgb (construction, setColor); GColumn (size, operator[], at(), init());
  t_circle (getAlphaValue, ==, !=, toString); GCanvas<8> construction,
  clear/reset, PPM output/load/round-trip (including comment/blank-line handling
  and all five error paths), diff (value, symmetry, scaling, dimension-mismatch),
  addTriangle(t_cart) (alpha=0/0.5/1, bounding-box exclusion),
  addTriangle(t_circle) (pixel coloring, DEBUG bad-angle guards), addTriangles
  (empty no-op), getAverageColors; GCanvas8/16/24 concrete classes (construction,
  color-depth constants, operator-, PPM round-trip).

- Comprehensive unit tests added for GCommonMathHelperFunctionsT and
  GCommonHelperFunctionsT in GCommonStandardTests.cpp. New tests cover:
  grational_sigmoid (zero, boundedness, antisymmetry, convergence, known
  values, DEBUG steepness guard); enforceRangeConstraint; checkRangeCompliance
  (fp and int); getWorstCase/getBestCase (bool and sortOrder overloads);
  checkValueRange (fp/int, open/closed boundaries, warnOnly); getMinMax (1D–4D);
  GMean; GStandardDeviation; PowSmallPosInt constexpr function; subtractVec;
  addVec; multVecConst; assignVecConst; sumTupleVec; squareSumTupleVec;
  productSumTupleVec; squareDeviation; getRegressionParameters; getRatioError;
  getRatioErrors; isClose; g_delete; g_array_delete; ptrDifferenceCheck (raw
  and shared_ptr); g_ptr_conversion (raw and shared_ptr); convertSmartPointer;
  vecToString; copyArrays; splitStringT (single and dual separator);
  getMapItem (mutable and const); to_string (integral, fp, scoped enum);
  erase_if; environmentVariableAs. DEBUG-only assertions are guarded with
  #ifdef DEBUG so the test suite is valid in both Debug and Release builds.

- Build script (prepareBuild.sh) overhauled. New options: --clean (interactively
  wipes the build directory, then exits — does not proceed to reconfigure);
  --dryrun (prints all CMake -D flags without configuring, useful for IDE setup);
  --generate-preset (writes a CMakeUserPresets.json to the current directory
  encoding all settings from the current .gcfg file, then exits without running
  cmake — the user copies the file to the project root so that IDEs such as CLion
  pick up the configuration automatically); --build (runs make -j$(nproc) after
  cmake configuration). --build may be combined with --clean and/or a .gcfg file:
  --build alone skips cmake when the directory is already configured and goes
  straight to make; --clean --build cleans, configures, then builds. When called
  without --clean in an already-configured directory the script prompts to clean
  before proceeding; if the user declines, it terminates.

- CMakePresets.json added. Provides a ready-made "geneva-default" preset that
  CLion and VS Code can pick up directly, eliminating the need to manually
  configure BOOST_ROOT and other paths in the IDE's CMake profile. For a
  configuration tailored to a specific .gcfg file, use
  prepareBuild.sh --generate-preset from the build directory, which writes a
  CMakeUserPresets.json there (not checked in) and exits without reconfiguring.
  Copy the file to the project root to activate it in the IDE.

- Deprecated Boost Phoenix headers replaced. The boost/spirit/include/phoenix_*.hpp
  shim headers (deprecated since Boost 1.66) are replaced with boost/phoenix/*.hpp
  in GFormulaParserT.hpp, GParameterPropertyParser.hpp, and GBaseClientT.hpp,
  removing a category of compiler warnings on Boost >= 1.90.

- Incremental Boost de-dependency (non-Serialization / non-Spirit / non-Asio):
  Numerous Boost headers that have direct C++ standard equivalents have been
  replaced across all five libraries:
  - boost::numeric_cast → Gem::Common::narrow_cast (checked cast using std::numeric_limits)
  - boost::checked_delete / boost::checked_array_delete → delete / delete[]
  - boost::iterator_facade → hand-written C++ forward iterator in GPtrVectorT.hpp
  - boost::variant (non-recursive codeEntry in GFormulaParserT) → std::variant
  - boost::uuids::random_generator → Gem::Common::generate_uuid_v4() (thread-local
    std::mt19937_64, RFC 4122 v4 UUID)
  - boost::tokenizer + boost::char_separator → std::string::find-based splitting
  - boost::trim → inline std::string::find_first/last_not_of whitespace trimming
  - boost::algorithm/string.hpp → removed from 15+ headers (all uses were stale)
  - boost::math::float_prior<T> / float_next<T> → std::nextafter (from <cmath>)
  - boost::math::constants::pi/e → std::numbers::pi/e (or numeric literals in CUDA paths)
  - boost::math::special_functions.hpp / next.hpp → removed (replaced by std::nextafter)
  - boost::numeric::bounds<T>::highest() / lowest() → std::numeric_limits<T>::max/lowest()
  - boost::limits.hpp → <limits>
  - boost::enable_shared_from_this → std::enable_shared_from_this (already used; include removed)
  - boost::exception / boost::diagnostic_information → removed; catch(boost::exception&)
    handlers were dead code (Geneva never throws boost::exception subtypes; Asio's
    system_error inherits from std::exception); replaced by std::exception catch-all
  - boost::predef (BOOST_COMP_GNUC < 5 guard) → dead code removed (Geneva requires GCC 13+)
  - boost::lambda/lambda.hpp → removed (stale include in GObject.hpp)
  - boost::cstdint.hpp in code-generation output → <cstdint>
  Remaining intentional Boost dependencies: Boost.Serialization, Boost.Asio/Beast
  (networking), Boost.Spirit+Phoenix+Fusion (formula parser, Priority 16 rewrite),
  Boost.ProgramOptions (command-line API), Boost.PropertyTree (JSON config),
  boost/config.hpp + boost/version.hpp (min-version enforcement in GGlobalDefines.hpp).

- Boost serialization macros annotated with // NOLINT. CLion/clangd incorrectly
  flagged BOOST_CLASS_EXPORT_IMPLEMENT, BOOST_CLASS_EXPORT_KEY, and related
  macros as missing semicolons. All instances now carry a // NOLINT comment.

- Gemfony branding removed from file headers.

- The common test executable was renamed from CommonStandardTests to GCommonStandardTests.

- The test framework has been migrated from Boost.Test to Catch2 v3. Boost.Test
  is no longer a build dependency. libcatch2-dev (>= 3.0) is now required when
  building with GENEVA_BUILD_TESTS=TRUE. The header
  include/geneva/tests/Geneva_tests.hpp is no longer part of the installed public
  API; it remains in the source tree for internal use by Geneva's own test drivers.
  Users writing tests against Geneva classes should use Catch2 directly.

- Static linking support removed (see INCOMPATIBILITIES above). The
  CMakeModules/CommonGenevaBuild.cmake and CMakeModules/IdentifySystemParameters.cmake
  files (and their copies under examples/*/CMakeModules/) have been simplified
  accordingly: the GENEVA_STATIC_FLAG_IN function parameter, the BUILD_SHARED_LIBS
  conditional, the Boost_USE_STATIC_LIBS conditional, and the optional dl/z library
  search on UNIX have all been removed.

- CUDA build improvements:
  - New SKIPALLCUDA / GENEVA_SKIP_CUDA option in genevaConfig.gcfg and prepareBuild.sh.
    When set to 1, all CUDA compilation is unconditionally disabled: example 15
    (GCUDAWorker), the CUDA benchmark (GCUDAOptBenchmark), and the optional CUDA RNG
    in Hap are excluded from the build even if nvcc is present on the system.
    GENEVA_USE_CUDA_RNG is force-overridden to OFF. Useful when the installed CUDA
    is broken or incompatible (e.g. CUDA 13.1 + glibc 2.39 rsqrt/noexcept mismatch).
  - New CUDA_NVCC / CUDA_ROOT variables in genevaConfig.gcfg and prepareBuild.sh.
    These allow pinning a specific CUDA toolkit version when multiple toolkits are
    installed side-by-side. CMAKE_CUDA_COMPILER is passed to CMake; CUDAToolkit_ROOT
    is automatically derived from it so find_package(CUDAToolkit) locates the
    matching headers and libraries.
  - find_package(CUDAToolkit) is now called after enable_language(CUDA) in the
    top-level CMakeLists.txt and in examples/geneva/15_GCUDAWorker/CMakeLists.txt.
    This makes CUDA::cudart an explicit link target for GCUDAWorker, fixing an
    "undefined reference to cudaGetDeviceProperties_v2" linker error that occurred
    with CUDA 12+ toolkits when multiple CUDA versions are installed.
  - NVCC diagnostic 20012 (spurious __host__/__device__ annotation warnings from
    Boost.Fusion headers) suppressed via -diag-suppress=20012, using the same
    $<$<COMPILE_LANGUAGE:CUDA>:...> generator expression as the existing suppressions
    for diagnostics 68, 186, and 191 — non-CUDA translation units are unaffected.
  - GImageBuilder.cpp: clockRate and memoryClockRate fields of cudaDeviceProp are
    guarded with #if CUDART_VERSION < 12000 — both were removed from the struct in
    CUDA 12.0.

- Fixed compilation issues for CUDA example, related to mismatch of compiler- and CUDA-versions.

- Removed GCommonMathHelperFunctions.hpp / GCommonMathHelperFunctions.cpp entirely. The ~20
  g-prefixed math wrappers (gsqrt, gpow, gfabs, gexp, glog, gmin, gmax, gfloor, gcos, gsin, …)
  they contained were redundant in C++20 and are now replaced with direct std:: calls at every
  call site. The header is no longer installed. The gmix wrapper is replaced with std::lerp
  (or its manual equivalent where nvcc is involved). The gsign wrapper, which was unused, has
  been deleted. The gsigmoid function, which implements a rational/algebraic softsign rather
  than a true sigmoid (f(x) = barrier·x / (steepness + |x|)), has been moved to
  GCommonMathHelperFunctionsT.hpp as a floating-point template renamed grational_sigmoid
  (the old name gsigmoid was misleading — this is a rational/algebraic softsign, not an
  exponential sigmoid) with a debug-mode precondition check for steepness > 0.
  Unit tests for grational_sigmoid are in GCommonStandardTests.

- GCanvas.hpp / GCanvas.cpp cleaned up and optimised:
  - Bug fix: dimension check in loadFromPPM() used `v[0] <= 0` on std::size_t
    (unsigned), which is always false. Fixed to `v[0] == 0 || v[1] == 0`.
  - Performance: diff31 / diff21 and the derived dot products (dot11, dot12,
    dot22, denom_inv) are triangle-invariant but were being recomputed for every
    pixel in the inner i_y loop of addTriangle(t_cart). They are now hoisted
    before the outer i_x loop.
  - Memory: virtual destructors removed from GRgb and GColumn (nothing inherits
    from them; the vtable pointer cost was 8 bytes per pixel — ~3.8 MB per
    800×600 canvas). BOOST_CLASS_EXPORT_KEY/IMPLEMENT removed from both types
    (serialized by value, not through base-class pointers, so export is a no-op).
  - Memory: NCOLORS and MAXCOLOR in GCanvas<> promoted from non-static instance
    members to static constexpr, eliminating one redundant copy per canvas object.
  - Performance: std::pow(x, 2.f) × 3 in diff() replaced with x*x.
  - Performance: push_back loop in reset() replaced with assign().
  - Cleanliness: duplicate standard headers removed (<cstdlib>, <vector>,
    <algorithm> each appeared twice; <list> was unused). boost/math/constants
    header removed; boost::math::constants::pi<float>() replaced with a local
    constexpr float two_pi_f (std::numbers unavailable in CUDA nvcc). using
    namespace std; removed from the
    loadFromPPM() method body (was polluting every including translation unit);
    all affected identifiers qualified with std::. Redundant using namespace
    Gem::Common; directives removed from diff() and addTriangle(t_cart) (both
    are already inside that namespace). C-style casts replaced with static_cast
    in toPPM() and getAverageColors(). Typo "addTriangel" fixed to "addTriangle"
    in the DEBUG error message. Dead comment "// Converts the three angles"
    removed.

- GCommonEnums.hpp / GCommonEnums.cpp cleaned up for C++20 compliance:
  - Unused includes removed from the header (<boost/cast.hpp>, <cmath>, <cstdio>,
    <cstdlib>); <boost/cast.hpp> moved to GCommonEnums.cpp where boost::numeric_cast
    is used. Files that previously relied on the transitive include now include
    <boost/cast.hpp> directly (GHapEnums.cpp, GCourtierEnums.cpp,
    GCourtierHelperFunctions.cpp, GThreadPool.cpp).
  - 9 namespace-scope `const` variables promoted to `constexpr` (DEFAULTBUFFERSIZE,
    CE_DEF_SIMILARITY_DIFFERENCE, DEFAULTNBINSGPD, VAR_IS_ESSENTIAL, VAR_IS_SECONDARY,
    CE_SILENT, CE_WITH_MESSAGES, DEFAULTNHARDWARETHREADS, DEFAULTMAXNHARDWARETHREADS).
    CE_DEF_SIMILARITY_DIFFERENCE was also simplified from pow(10., -5) to the literal 1e-5.
  - Dead enum value parameter_source::SIZE removed (it equalled ASSIGNMENT rather than
    ASSIGNMENT+1, making it useless as a range sentinel; grep confirmed no usage outside
    its own definition).
  - Missing operator<< / operator>> for dimensions added to GCommonEnums.cpp (the
    declarations existed in the header but the definitions were absent).
  - Typo in serModeToString: "unkown" → "unknown"; dead break-after-return statements
    removed.
  - [[nodiscard]] added to serModeToString declaration.
  - GCourtierEnums.hpp: boost::uint32_t replaced with std::uint32_t (three constants);
    <cstdint> added; const → constexpr for the three affected constants.
  - GMPIConsumerT.hpp: boost::uint32_t replaced with std::uint32_t; <cstdint> added.
  - GOptimizationEnums.hpp: boost::numeric::bounds<T>::highest() / ::lowest() replaced
    with std::numeric_limits<T>::max() (already included via <limits>); the three
    affected constants promoted from const to constexpr.

- GGlobalDefines.hpp is no longer generated from a CMake template at build time.
  The file GGlobalDefines.hpp.in has been deleted; GGlobalDefines.hpp is now a
  regular, manually maintained header checked directly into the repository.
  The two macros it defines (GENEVA_VERSION and MIN_BOOST_VERSION) carry inline
  comments explaining their encoding and pointing to the authoritative locations
  (VERSION_MAJOR/MINOR/PATCH in CMakeLists.txt and GENEVA_MIN_BOOST_VERSION in
  CMakeModules/CommonGenevaBuild.cmake). CMakeLists.txt likewise points back to
  GGlobalDefines.hpp for the required manual update. The CONFIGURE_FILE call and
  the associated string-manipulation logic have been removed from
  include/common/CMakeLists.txt.

- GBarrier.hpp removed. The single usage site (GBufferPortTTest.cpp) has been
  updated to use std::latch (C++20, <latch>) instead. std::latch::arrive_and_wait()
  replaces GBarrier::wait() directly; std::latch is the appropriate type here
  since the barrier was used as a one-shot "starting gun" (each thread calls it
  exactly once). For reusable cross-generation barriers, std::barrier would be
  the equivalent C++20 standard type.

- Several concurrency and logic bugs fixed across the Common, Hap, Courtier, Geneva,
  and Geneva-Individuals libraries (identified by manual code review):
  - GGlobalOptionsT::remove(): two bugs corrected simultaneously — the key parameter
    was commented out and never used, and the iterator was set to kvp_.end() instead
    of kvp_.find(key), so the function never deleted anything and always returned false.
  - GGlobalOptionsT::getContentVector(): parameter changed from by-value to by-reference;
    the old by-value signature silently discarded all push_back results, leaving the
    caller's vector always unchanged.
  - GBoundedBufferT::try_pop_copy() / try_pop_move(): both functions notified not_empty_
    after removing an element instead of not_full_, permanently blocking producers
    waiting for space under high load when only the non-blocking pop variants were used.
  - GThreadGroup::clearThreads(): missing mutex guard added; all other methods of the
    class already held the mutex before accessing the thread container.
  - GCUDARng (CUDA path): rewritten with persistent curandState allocation and proper
    non-deterministic seeding via GRandomFactory::getSeed(). The previous implementation
    re-allocated and re-initialized states on every batch using a hard-coded seed of 1234,
    causing every batch to produce the identical sequence.
  - GCUDARng::stop_ changed from plain bool to std::atomic<bool> to make the
    multi-threaded access safe by type.
  - baseScanParT copy constructor: nSteps_(cp.step_) corrected to nSteps_(cp.nSteps_).
    The copy-paste error caused copied scan objects to have a wrong step count,
    making the parameter scan terminate after the first step (when step_==0 at copy time).
  - GSimulatedAnnealing::setTDegradationStrength(): validation widened from alpha > 0
    to alpha in (0, 1). Values >= 1 produce a non-convergent SA (temperature constant
    or rising). A temperature floor of std::numeric_limits<double>::min() is now applied
    in updateTemperature() to prevent division by zero / NaN propagation in saProb().
  - GSwarmAlgorithm::pruneVelocity(): the guard checking dbl_vel_max_cnt_[i] > 0 was
    inside #ifdef DEBUG; moved outside so Release builds also catch a zero velocity-max
    (which caused silent division by zero, collapsing all velocities to zero).
  - GBrokerT::finalize(): the consumer shutdown loop now runs inside the
    consumerEnrolmentMutex lock, eliminating a data race with concurrent
    enrol_consumer() calls that could push_back to the same vector simultaneously.
  - GBrokerT::enrol_consumer() / enrol_consumer_vec(): the consumersPresent_ check
    was moved inside the lock to eliminate a TOCTOU race that allowed two concurrent
    callers to both pass the check and each register a consumer.
  - GBrokerT::enrol_buffer_port(): a stray std::cout replaced with glogger.
  - GSerialConsumerT::setup(): enrol_consumer_vec() corrected to enrol_consumer()
    (enrol_consumer_vec expects a std::vector, not a single shared_ptr; the template
    instantiation error was latent and would only appear when setup() was actually called).
  - GSerialConsumerT::shutdown_(): processingThread_.join() is now guarded with
    joinable(), preventing std::system_error when shutdown is called before
    async_startProcessing_() was ever invoked.
  - GExternalEvaluatorIndividual::fitnessCalculation(): a RAII TempFileGuard was added
    directly after the three IPC file names are computed, ensuring the files are cleaned
    up (respecting the remove_exec_temporaries_ flag) even when an exception is thrown
    before reaching the end of the function. std::filesystem::remove is a no-op for
    non-existent files, so the guard is safe for result files that the external program
    never created.
  - GExternalEvaluatorIndividual: three setXxxRange() error messages (setDeltaRange,
    setSigma1Range, setSigma2Range) printed the value of max instead of min when
    reporting that min was negative.
  - GNeuralNetworkIndividual::trainingSet::compare(): the Output[] loop used nInputNodes
    as its bound instead of nOutputNodes, causing out-of-bounds reads (UB) whenever the
    two counts differ.

- Obsolete Boost version guards removed. Geneva requires Boost 1.90+, making all
  #if BOOST_VERSION < X conditionals for Boost releases prior to 1.90 dead code:
  - GPODVectorT.hpp, GPtrVectorT.hpp: Boost 1.58 serialization workaround
    (data.clear() on load) removed.
  - GWebsocketConsumerT.hpp: ws_.write_buffer_size() fallback for Boost < 1.70 removed;
    ws_.write_buffer_bytes() is now unconditional.
  - GExternalEvaluatorIndividual.cpp: xml_writer_settings<char> fallback for
    Boost <= 1.55 removed; xml_writer_settings<std::string> is now unconditional.
  - GGlobalDefines.hpp: NOMINMAX / WIN32_LEAN_AND_MEAN workaround for a Boost 1.70
    Beast bug on Windows removed.

- Multi-mutex locking modernized. Three sites that used the verbose
  unique_lock + std::defer_lock + std::lock() pattern have been replaced with
  std::scoped_lock, which provides identical deadlock-avoidance semantics with
  less boilerplate: GBrokerT::finalize() (three mutexes), GBrokerT::enrol_buffer_port()
  (two mutexes), GThreadPool::setNThreads() (two mutexes). Sites that explicitly
  unlock before a condition_variable notify_all() (enrol_consumer, enrol_consumer_vec)
  retain unique_lock as scoped_lock has no unlock() method.

- GCommonHelperFunctionsT.hpp overhauled: 12 unused or dead functions removed
  (copySmartPointer, copySmartPointerVector, convertSimplePointer — which also
  contained a latent dynamic_cast bug — g_ptr_conversion, assert_sizes_match_container,
  assert_container_sizes_match, erase_according_to_flags,
  forcedSubmissionToBoostLockfree, timedSubmissionToBoostLockfree,
  forcedRetrievalFromBoostLockfree, timedRetrievalFromBoostLockfree, vector_as_string),
  along with the two Boost.Lockfree includes they required. Remaining changes:
  boost::optional replaced with std::optional in environmentVariableAs;
  g_make_unique replaced with std::make_unique at its sole call site and deleted;
  Gem::Common::erase_if replaced with std::erase_if in pure-C++ translation units
  (the local implementation is retained for CUDA-visible headers where nvcc lacks
  this C++20 addition). Style updated throughout: range-based for loops, auto
  iterator types, std::make_shared, shorter error messages.

- GCommonMathHelperFunctionsT.hpp overhauled:
  * GVecStandardDeviation removed (unused).
  * Unused named boolean constants GWARNINGONLY, GERRORONLY, GFWARNONLY,
    GINTLOWERCLOSED, GINTLOWEROPEN, GINTUPPERCLOSED, and GINTUPPEROPEN removed.
  * PowSmallPosInt<B,E> struct replaced with a constexpr function template of the
    same name (call sites updated: PowSmallPosInt<B,E>::result → PowSmallPosInt<B,E>()).
    Compatible with nvcc (uses if constexpr, not consteval).
  * getMinMax(1D) rewritten using std::minmax_element; 4D overload docstring
    corrected ("3d" → "4d").
  * GMean: iterator loop replaced with range-based for; boost::numeric_cast
    replaced with static_cast.
  * GStandardDeviation: redundant empty-check removed (GMean already guards it);
    iterator loop replaced with range-based for; std::sqrt used explicitly;
    GSQUARED macro replaced with d*d.
  * subtractVec / addVec: iterator loops replaced with std::transform; stale
    "Subtract" comment in addVec corrected.
  * multVecConst: iterator loop replaced with range-based for.
  * assignVecConst: iterator loop replaced with std::fill.
  * sumTupleVec: iterator loop replaced with range-based for; double semicolon fixed.
  * squareSumTupleVec: iterator loop replaced with range-based for;
    std::pow(x, 2.) replaced with x*x.
  * productSumTupleVec: iterator loop replaced with range-based for.
  * squareDeviation: iterator loop replaced with range-based for; std::pow(d, 2.)
    replaced with d*d.
  * getRegressionParameters: repeated std::pow(sum_x, 2.) calls replaced with a
    shared denom variable (sum_x*sum_x).
  * getRatioError: typo "ne" → "be" in comment; std::pow(x, 2.) replaced with
    explicit intermediate variables.
  * getRatioErrors: iterator loop replaced with index-based for; reserve() added.

- GCommonInterfaceT<g_class_type> overhauled for C++20 compliance and correctness:
  - Exception safety: fromStream() now wraps the raw pointer returned by
    Boost.Serialization in a std::unique_ptr before calling load_(), ensuring the
    allocated object is destroyed if load_() throws.  g_delete() is no longer called
    at the call site.  The same fix was applied to the only other raw-pointer
    Boost.Serialization pattern in the codebase (networkData::loadFromDisk()).
  - #include <sstream> added (std::ostringstream / std::istringstream were used
    without it; the include was previously satisfied transitively).
  - SFINAE enable_if constraints on clone<T>(), load(shared_ptr), and load(ref)
    replaced with C++20 requires-clauses (requires std::is_base_of_v<…>).
  - Small scalar parameters (serializationMode, expectation, double limit) are now
    passed by value instead of const-reference in toStream(), fromStream(),
    toString(), fromString(), toFile(), fromFile(), compare(), and compare_().
  - Redundant std::ofstream::close() / std::ifstream::close() calls removed from
    toFile() and fromFile() (the streams close automatically on scope exit).
  - Redundant std::filesystem::path(p) wrapping removed from fromFile() (p is
    already a path).
  - Debug check in toFile() changed from post-close std::filesystem::exists() to
    ofstr.good() checked while the stream is still open — the old check could not
    reliably detect write errors.
  - G_API_GENEVA on the three unit-test virtual methods (modify_GUnitTests_(),
    specificTestsNoFailureExpected_GUnitTests_(), specificTestsFailuresExpected_
    GUnitTests_()) corrected to G_API_COMMON (the methods are declared in the
    Common library, not the Geneva library).

- The vestigial BASE macro (#define BASE, which expanded to nothing) has been
  removed from GGlobalDefines.hpp and all 40 files that used it across the common,
  courtier, and geneva libraries.  The macro was a pre-C++11 documentation
  convention indicating the first pure-virtual declaration of a method; it has been
  superseded by override and final keywords and carried no semantic value.

- prepareBuild.sh: new -y / --yes flag skips the interactive "Proceed? [y/N]"
  confirmation that --clean (and reconfiguring an already-configured directory)
  would otherwise require. Intended for use in scripts and CI pipelines where no
  terminal is available. The flag is accepted both as -y and --yes; it affects all
  code paths that call _confirm_and_clean.

- clang-tidy code-quality pass across the entire codebase (~256 files). Fixes
  cover priorities 1–3 of the project's clang-tidy configuration: modernise-use-
  override, performance-unnecessary-copy-initialization, readability-qualified-auto,
  cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-member-init, and related categories. No functional
  changes; all fixes are mechanical correctness and readability improvements that
  leave the public API unchanged.

- clang-format normalization across all 325 .cpp/.hpp files. The entire source tree
  now conforms to the project's .clang-format configuration. One substantive fix
  included: a missing <boost/numeric/conversion/bounds.hpp> include in
  GConstrainedValueLimitT.hpp that had been satisfied transitively was made direct.

- GCUDARng bug fix: the CUDA-based random number generator (GCudaRNG, available
  when USECUDARNG is enabled) previously re-initialized its cuRAND PRNG state on
  every batch with a hardcoded seed (1234), causing every batch to produce the same
  sequence of random numbers. The fix allocates curandState on the GPU once at
  construction time, seeds it from GRandomFactory::getSeed() (the same source used
  by the CPU-based RNG path), and advances the persistent state on each batch call
  via curand() without re-initialization. A dedicated cudaStream_t is now used for
  all RNG kernel launches and transfers so that the RNG producer thread does not
  compete with fitness-evaluation kernels on the default stream.

- GGlobalOptionsT / GTupleIO: missing direct includes added. GGlobalOptionsT.hpp
  now includes <string> and <vector> directly; GTupleIO.hpp includes <sstream>
  directly. Both headers had been relying on transitive includes from other Geneva
  headers, which caused compilation failures when they were included in isolation.

- New GContainerT<T, StoragePolicy> class added (include/common/GContainerT.hpp).
  GContainerT is a unified, storage-policy-based generic container that subsumes the
  functionality of GPODVectorT and GPtrVectorT while adding C++20 modernisations and
  support for alternative backends beyond std::vector. Both legacy classes remain
  untouched; GContainerT is a new component intended to pave the migration path.
  Key design points:
  * Two storage policies: PodStorage<T, Container> for POD types (deep copy by
    value assignment) and SharedPtrStorage<T, Container> for polymorphic Geneva
    objects held via shared_ptr (deep copy via the clone()/load() protocol).
  * The Container template parameter (default: std::vector) allows any compatible
    STL sequence container, e.g. std::deque or Boost containers. Convenience
    aliases GPodContainer<T, Container> and GPtrContainer<T, Container> are provided.
  * Four C++20 concepts gate method availability at compile time:
    HasContiguousStorage (data()), HasCapacity (reserve/capacity/shrinkToFit),
    HasRandomAccess (crossOver, operator<=>), HasFrontInsertion (pushFront/popFront/
    emplaceFront). Methods not supported by the chosen container are excluded from the
    overload set via requires-clauses, yielding clear compiler errors rather than
    link failures.
  * The conversion_iterator inner class from GPtrVectorT is superseded by filteredView<
    DerivedType>(), a lazy C++20 range view (std::views::transform | std::views::filter)
    that yields only elements dynamically castable to DerivedType. The eager
    attachViewTo<DerivedType>() variant is retained for callers that require a
    materialised vector.
  * Full Boost.Serialization integration including is_abstract specialisations.
  * Complete Doxygen documentation on all classes, concepts, policies, methods,
    and data members.
  * Catch2 v3 unit tests (GContainerTTests) cover 97 % of the implementation
    (261 assertions across four test groups: [pod][vector], [pod][deque],
    [ptr][vector], [edge]).
  * Benchmark program GContainerTBenchmark supports --mode pod|ptr|fuzz|all,
    --container vector|deque|all, --size, --duration, --seed, and --quick (short
    smoke-test run); the benchmark is excluded from ctest.

- C++20 modernisation of three member-detection type traits in GTypeTraitsT.hpp:
  has_compare_member<T>, has_clone_member<T>, and has_load_member<T> previously used
  a pre-C++11 SFINAE pattern (decltype(&C::member) in an overload set, sized via
  char/long sentinel types). All three are now implemented with C++20 requires-
  expressions (requires { &T::member; }). The ::value API is preserved; no call
  sites needed updating (the traits are not used internally by Geneva).
  <concepts> added to the include list.

- GRandomT.hpp: GRandomT::getThreadId() return type simplified from
  decltype(std::this_thread::get_id()) to the canonical std::thread::id. No
  behavioural change; the type was always std::thread::id.

- GFormulaParserT.hpp: five BOOST_ASSERT(0) calls in the AST-compiler visitor
  (unreachable branches of the operator(), unary_function_, binary_function_,
  and signed_ overloads) replaced with assert(false && "unreachable: unknown
  operator/function in AST visitor"). <cassert> added to the include list.
  BOOST_ASSERT is no longer referenced in GFormulaParserT.hpp; the Boost.Assert
  header is no longer transitively included from this file.

- Clang build support added. The build system now supports Clang (>= 18, default)
  alongside GCC (>= 13) as an alternative C++ compiler. Compiler selection is
  controlled by the COMPILER variable in genevaConfig.gcfg ("clang", "gcc", or ""
  to let CMake choose). prepareBuild.sh resolves the variable to the actual
  clang/clang++ or gcc/g++ executables found in PATH and passes
  -DCMAKE_C_COMPILER / -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER to CMake. CMakeUserPresets.json
  (--generate-preset) also encodes the selected compiler. The following Clang-
  specific warnings that were latent under GCC are now fixed:
  * GMPIConsumerT.hpp (three sites): constructor initializer-list order corrected
    to match the class member declaration order (-Wreorder-ctor).
  * GCourtierHelperFunctions.cpp: missing STOP case added to the pcToStr() switch
    over networked_consumer_payload_command (-Wswitch).
  * GAsioConsumerT.hpp, GWebsocketConsumerT.hpp: redundant std::move() removed
    from boost::asio::ip::tcp::endpoint{} temporaries (-Wpessimizing-move).
  * GSerialConsumerT.hpp: redundant std::move() removed from std::thread{}
    temporary (-Wpessimizing-move).
  Separately, libgemfony-courtier and libgemfony-geneva now declare
  TARGET_LINK_LIBRARIES(… MPI::MPI_CXX) when GENEVA_BUILD_WITH_MPI_CONSUMER is
  enabled — Clang's linker is stricter than GCC about unresolved symbols in
  shared libraries. This is a correctness fix; the GCC build was relying on
  lazy symbol resolution that is not portable.

